{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE PAGE SHELL — every rebuilt public page extends this
  Phase 1 (the shell) and Phase 2 (the chrome) of design_handoff_africa_gates
  REFERENCE §6.7 · §7.1–§7.5 · §10 · §13
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  The root is 100dvh and does not scroll; `<main class="ag-main">` is the only scroller,
  so every bar is a plain flex child that cannot move with the content.

  ── THE CHROME IS THE LAYOUT'S, NOT EACH PAGE'S ─────────────────────────────

  A page gets the whole of the shared chrome by extending this file and saying three
  things about itself, as variables set at the top of the page template:

    app_bar    {variant:'root'|'child', title, sub, back, share, search, avatar}
               — the phone app bar (§7.2). Default: root, titled with page_heading or
               page_title. A tab destination is root; a pushed screen is child.
    tab        'home' | 'discover' | 'nominate' | 'pulse' — the active tab (§7.3).
               Unset means none is lit, which is right for every page that is not a tab
               destination.
    flow_page  true on a flow (vote, checkout, event detail, nominee, product): no tab
               bar — that page brings its own back button and bottom action bar (§7.3).

  The blocks remain for a page that needs to replace a piece outright, but a partial
  every page must remember to include is a partial the next page forgets — which is how
  the old layout came to mount Quick settings on 180 pages with no button to open it
  (ChromeReachabilityTest). So the defaults ARE the chrome.

  What each breakpoint shows is CSS, not markup chosen per request (REFERENCE §6.7):
  below 600 the app bar and the tab bar; from 600 the site header. The Menu and Quick
  settings are phone sheets; the search palette and the shortcuts dialog answer `/` and
  `?` at any width.

  ── WHERE THIS DIFFERS FROM snippets/twig/page-shell.twig ─────────────────

  · `<html class="ag-shelled">` arms the overflow lock, scoped rather than global
    (Phase 1 deviation #1).
  · `lang`/`dir` are `lang()`/`lang_dir()`, LanguageMiddleware's one answer — the
    snippet's `lang == 'ar'` would be a second resolver for one value.
  · Colour is `ag_accents()` in a nonced <style> BEFORE the stylesheets (GAPS §8 Q1).
  · There is no `partials/nav.twig`. The header is `partials/site-header.twig`; Gee is
    `partials/gee.twig` (Phase 3), mounted in the `gee` block below.

  ── THE FLASH RAIL IS HERE BECAUSE A REDIRECT WITH NOTHING ON THE OTHER END IS SILENT ─

  `flash_error`/`flash_ok`/`flash_notice` are written by public POST handlers that then
  redirect. The old layout's rail was destroyed with it (inventory: _partials.md, MUST
  RESTORE), so every such message reached nobody. A page that places its own sets
  `own_flash` and the rail stands aside, or the message appears twice.
#}
{% set _bar = {variant: 'root', title: page_heading|default(page_title|default('Africa GATES'))}|merge(app_bar|default({})) %}
{% set _member_sync = is_member ? (member_display() is null ? 'empty' : 'saved') : '' %}
{# Preferences (CookiePrefs): may the display store outlive the tab? The one fact about
   consent a script needs, handed over as a value rather than the whole record. #}
{% set _consent = consent() %}
{# Gee (Phase 3, REFERENCE §7.7): on every shell page except Pulse. Also not on the support
   pages — the desk's own ticket list and forms are there, and two launchers onto one
   brain is a choice nobody can make (the old layout's reason, still true) — nor on a page
   that hides the chrome. Hoisted to template scope: it is read by the head, the `gee`
   block and the scripts. #}
{% set _gee_off = hide_chrome|default(false)
                  or gates_page|default('') in ['pulse', 'support']
                  or tab|default('') == 'pulse' %}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ lang() }}" dir="{{ lang_dir() }}" class="ag-shelled"
      data-ag-easy-font="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Atkinson+Hyperlegible:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;1,400&amp;display=swap"
      data-ag-keep="{{ _consent and _consent.remember ? '1' : '0' }}"
      {% if _member_sync %}data-ag-sync="{{ _member_sync }}"{% endif %}>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  {# `viewport-fit=cover`, or every `env(safe-area-inset-*)` resolves to zero. #}
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
  <title>{{ page_title|default('Africa GATES') }}</title>
  {% if meta_description is defined %}<meta name="description" content="{{ meta_description }}">{% endif %}
  {% if meta_robots is defined %}<meta name="robots" content="{{ meta_robots }}">{% endif %}
  {# Only for a signed-in member: the token a11y.js sends with POST /account/display. #}
  {# …and on a page that posts by script with no session to speak of (the account-free
     support-ticket link, Phase 9): `csrf_meta`, so the token comes from this one tag. #}
  {% if _member_sync or csrf_meta|default(false) %}<meta name="ag-csrf" content="{{ csrf_token }}">{% endif %}

  {# Before any stylesheet — see the partial for why. #}
  {% block a11y_head %}{% include 'partials/a11y-head.twig' %}{% endblock %}

  {# §6.2: Playfair Display 700, DM Sans 400–700, JetBrains Mono 500/700, swap. #}
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Playfair+Display:wght@700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@500;700&display=swap">

  <style nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}">{{ ag_accents()|raw }}</style>

  {# In cascade order, the same order as AssetBundle::STYLESHEETS: the tokens, the
     shell, the base components, then the shared chrome (Phase 2). #}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/tokens.css') }}">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/shell.css') }}">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/components.css') }}">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/components/chrome.css') }}">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/components/menu-sheet.css') }}">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/components/consent.css') }}">
  {# The field macros' sheet (partials/field.twig): error, hint, counter and summary. Beside
     form-validate.js below, because a form saying `novalidate data-ag-validate` turns the
     browser's messages off on the promise that these replace them (FormErrorStateTest). #}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/components/forms.css') }}">
  {# Every image slot with no upload draws a default cover or avatar (DEFAULT-GRAPHICS §2). #}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/components/cover.css') }}">
  {% if not hide_chrome|default(false) %}<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/components/footer.css') }}">{% endif %}
  {% if not _gee_off %}<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/components/gee.css') }}">{% endif %}
  {% block head_styles %}{% endblock %}
</head>
<body data-page="{{ page_id|default('') }}">
  <a class="ag-skip" href="#main">{{ 'Skip to content'|trans }}</a>

  <div class="ag-shell">
    {% block header %}{% include 'partials/site-header.twig' %}{% endblock %}
    {% block app_bar %}{% include 'partials/app-bar.twig' with _bar only %}{% endblock %}

    <main class="ag-main" id="main">
      {% if not own_flash|default(false) %}{% include 'partials/flash.twig' %}{% endif %}
      {% block content %}{% endblock %}
      {# The site's only footer (Phase 4), inside the scroller so it is reached by scrolling
         and pinned to nothing. Not on a page that hides the chrome. #}
      {% block footer %}{% if not hide_chrome|default(false) %}{% include 'partials/site-footer.twig' %}{% endif %}{% endblock %}
    </main>

    {# The cookie notice, the preferences sheet and the "saved" line (§7.9). Inside the
       column on purpose: on a phone the notice is a flex child above the tab bar, so the
       scroller shrinks for it and it can cover nothing (see consent.css). #}
    {% include 'partials/cookie-consent.twig' %}

    {% block bottom_bar %}
      {% if not flow_page|default(false) %}{% include 'partials/tab-bar.twig' with { active: tab|default('') } only %}{% endif %}
    {% endblock %}
  </div>

  {# Gee — the guide everywhere, the help desk where somebody arrives stuck (§7.7, §8.22).
     Outside the column: the launcher and the panel are fixed, and clear every bottom bar
     through `--ag-bottom-ui` rather than by being placed in the flow. #}
  {% block gee %}{% if not _gee_off %}{% include 'partials/gee.twig' %}{% endif %}{% endblock %}

  {# Each starts `inert` (or `hidden`) and is opened by a control the chrome above draws
     — ChromeReachabilityTest holds that every one has a way in. #}
  {% block sheets %}
    {% include 'partials/menu-sheet.twig' %}
    {% include 'partials/quick-settings.twig' %}
    {% include 'partials/site-search.twig' %}
    {% include 'partials/shortcuts.twig' %}
  {% endblock %}

  <script defer src="{{ asset('/assets/js/shell.js') }}"></script>
  <script defer src="{{ asset('/assets/js/a11y.js') }}"></script>
  <script defer src="{{ asset('/assets/js/chrome.js') }}"></script>
  {# After chrome.js, whose `AGChrome.openSheet` it opens through (defer keeps the order). #}
  <script defer src="{{ asset('/assets/js/menu-sheet.js') }}"></script>
  <script defer src="{{ asset('/assets/js/header.js') }}"></script>
  <script defer src="{{ asset('/assets/js/search.js') }}"></script>
  <script defer src="{{ asset('/assets/js/consent.js') }}"></script>
  {% if not _gee_off %}<script defer src="{{ asset('/assets/js/gee.js') }}"></script>{% endif %}
  {# The shared validator: a form here that says `novalidate data-ag-validate` has
     turned the browser's own messages off on the promise this replaces them. #}
  <script defer src="{{ asset('/assets/js/form-validate.js') }}"></script>
  {% block foot_scripts %}{% endblock %}
</body>
</html>
